==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Power Backhoe Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Neo Backhoe Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Backhoe Cat's unique trait is that he can reliably target Metal enemies while ignoring other traits that may get in the way, but, if not for that, his stats make him a rather unreliable and inefficient Critical Hitter compared to others. Unless you have nothing better, it's best not to use him in purely Metal stages, but rather only in stages with Metal as support. A good example is [[Catfruit Jubilee]], in which Backhoe Cat is able to reliably target [[Metal Hippoe]] and possibly kill it, while about every other Critical Hitter without Area Attack might perform slightly worse.

He can still help in Metal-only stages as support, but never as your main Critical Hitter, for his attack rate and Critical chance are too low to be reliable. [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] can outperform him under most conditions, thanks to its recharge. However, on more frugal stages, Backhoe Cat's Money Up ability will put him on top; and due to his recharge time, you don't need to spam him, unlike Catasaurus, meaning he won't drain your cash. However, many other cats outperform him later on, including but not limited to: [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]], with his quick attack rate; Catasaurus and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], mainly with spammability; [[Crazed Moneko (Special Cat)|Crazed Moneko]], [[Sunny Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Sunny Neneko]] and [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cheerleader Cat]] with their 100% chance to perform Critical Hits and [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Marine Cat]] or [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Volley Cat]], with their higher ranges.

Backhoe, however, does possess a combo with Li'l Whale Cat for a 1% Critical chance boost. While this still isn't impressive on its own, it can be paired with others like [[Miracle Performance (Combo)|Miracle Performance]] and those provided by [[Sakura Sonic (Uber Rare Cat)|Sakura Sonic]]'s Ultra Form for greater effect.

==='''True Form'''===
Neo Backhoe Cat gains a chance to produce a Lv.1 [[Surge Attack]]. However, the Surge is not guaranteed, so the chance of both a Critical Hit and a Surge Attack happening at the same time is even lower, only a 7.5% chance. To make matters even worse, it has a very wide spawn area, so, even if Neo Backhoe Cat does both a Critical Hit and a Surge Attack, it may either miss completely or hit the enemies square in the face. Because of the way the Surge mechanic works, provided he does Critical, Surge, and the Surge spawns near or on the enemies; the following Critical functions as an Area Attack. Overall, a True Form best for gamblers.

